It is a Dooya Zigbee module that work on Tuya Zigbee. It is connected to the blinds via RJ11 cables from Dooya motor. I've tried the adding the new device by simply clone your github and adding the manufacturer ID and model ID to the device json file. I'm able to add from homey app after that. From homey app run console I can see the status updates and commands to the module showing no error. However, controlling from the homey app doesn't yield a physical response from the motor (I do see the logs sending the commands successfully. When I use the motor remote to control, I can see zigbee status updates processed by the app but no updates on UI.

